{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1765480,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"Veritas Clash - British Parliamentary Debate","festival_id":520986,"organization_id":825345,"web_url":"yugaantar.org\/","start_date":"2026-10-03T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-11-25T20:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/veritas-clash-british-parliamentary-debate-yugaantar-26-scaler-school-of-technology-bengaluru-karnataka-1765480","region":"online","details":"<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"296\" data-end=\"318\"><strong data-start=\"296\" data-end=\"318\">Veritas Clash:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-start=\"320\" data-end=\"367\">\n<li data-section-id=\"pzge50\" data-start=\"320\" data-end=\"367\"><strong data-start=\"322\" data-end=\"334\">Tagline:<\/strong> The arena of reason and rhetoric<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"369\" data-end=\"385\"><strong data-start=\"369\" data-end=\"385\">Description:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-start=\"387\" data-end=\"672\">\n<li data-section-id=\"176apg\" data-start=\"387\" data-end=\"544\">A British Parliamentary style debate competition where teams showcase critical thinking, communication skills, and logical reasoning through live arguments<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"pzrw4a\" data-start=\"545\" data-end=\"672\">Teams will present structured arguments, rebuttals, and closing remarks on a given motion to convince judges and the audience<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"674\" data-end=\"684\"><strong data-start=\"674\" data-end=\"684\">Theme:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-start=\"686\" data-end=\"997\">\n<li data-section-id=\"yhapfn\" data-start=\"686\" data-end=\"807\">Teams will debate on geopolitics, social issues, or fest-themed topics (motions announced 15 minutes before the debate)<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"17asfqh\" data-start=\"808\" data-end=\"851\">The medium of debate will be English only<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"13gqrdz\" data-start=\"852\" data-end=\"997\">Each team&rsquo;s bench (Opening Government, Closing Government, Opening Opposition, Closing Opposition) will be assigned by the organizing committee<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"999\" data-end=\"1020\"><strong data-start=\"999\" data-end=\"1020\">Team Composition:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-start=\"1022\" data-end=\"1250\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1g4n817\" data-start=\"1022\" data-end=\"1064\"><strong data-start=\"1024\" data-end=\"1034\">Teams:<\/strong> 2 participants per team (SS2)<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"sj2nv1\" data-start=\"1065\" data-end=\"1109\"><strong data-start=\"1067\" data-end=\"1084\">Adjudicators:<\/strong> Individual participation<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"vwkwg5\" data-start=\"1110\" data-end=\"1250\"><strong data-start=\"1112\" data-end=\"1122\">Roles:<\/strong> Each speaker has a designated role (PM, Deputy PM, Govt Member, Govt Whip, Opp Leader, Deputy Opp Leader, Opp Member, Opp Whip)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"1252\" data-end=\"1277\"><strong data-start=\"1252\" data-end=\"1277\">Performance Duration:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-start=\"1279\" data-end=\"1569\">\n<li data-section-id=\"alhvpp\" data-start=\"1279\" data-end=\"1344\">Research Phase: 15 minutes (after receiving motion\/info slides)<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1i2lb7e\" data-start=\"1345\" data-end=\"1388\">Setup Time: 1 minute before speech begins<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"13e0xvz\" data-start=\"1389\" data-end=\"1477\">Speaking Time per Team: 7 minutes (protected time: 1st &amp; 7th minute; 30-second buffer)<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"oj0y5j\" data-start=\"1478\" data-end=\"1504\">Deliberation: 15 minutes<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"4hh513\" data-start=\"1505\" data-end=\"1536\">Oral Adjudication: 10 minutes<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"v2h5nf\" data-start=\"1537\" data-end=\"1569\"><strong data-start=\"1539\" data-end=\"1560\">Total per Debate:<\/strong> ~2 hours<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"1571\" data-end=\"1610\"><strong data-start=\"1571\" data-end=\"1610\">Judging Criteria (100 Marks Total):<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-start=\"1612\" data-end=\"1774\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1mjvhwy\" data-start=\"1612\" data-end=\"1631\">Matter: 40 points<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1nqprg2\" data-start=\"1632\" data-end=\"1651\">Manner: 40 points<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"xuqcz4\" data-start=\"1652\" data-end=\"1671\">Method: 20 points<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"6io1ji\" data-start=\"1672\" data-end=\"1774\">Refer to the WUDC Debating &amp; Judging Manual for a detailed guide to the British Parliamentary format<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"1776\" data-end=\"1802\"><strong data-start=\"1776\" data-end=\"1802\">Submission Guidelines:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-start=\"1804\" data-end=\"1958\">\n<li data-section-id=\"x6ey9p\" data-start=\"1804\" data-end=\"1872\">Colleges sending <strong data-start=\"1823\" data-end=\"1828\">n<\/strong> teams must also send <strong data-start=\"1850\" data-end=\"1859\">n &ndash; 1<\/strong> adjudicators<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"111aabi\" data-start=\"1873\" data-end=\"1958\">Adjudicator registration must be done as a team of 1, named <strong data-start=\"1935\" data-end=\"1958\">ADJUDICATOR_&lt;Name&gt;<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\" data-start=\"1960\" data-end=\"1982\"><strong data-start=\"1960\" data-end=\"1982\">Strict Compliance:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-start=\"1984\" data-end=\"2136\">\n<li data-section-id=\"ttcvs7\" data-start=\"1984\" data-end=\"2080\">Failure to follow these registration and submission guidelines will result in disqualification<\/li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1axnlgc\" data-start=\"2081\" data-end=\"2136\">Kindly ensure all instructions are carefully followed<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":"Cash prizes and certificates for winners, runners-up, second runner-up, and Best Speaker.","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":28043294,"moderation